    "title": "pandas.Timestamp.tzname — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Timestamp.tzname#\n\n- Timestamp.tzname()#\n- Return time zone name. This method returns the name of the Timestamp’s time zone as a string. See also \n  - `Timestamp.tzinfo`\n  - Returns the timezone information of the Timestamp.\n  - `Timestamp.tz_convert`\n  - Convert timezone-aware Timestamp to another time zone.\n Examples >>> ts = pd.Timestamp('2023-01-01 10:00:00', tz='Europe/Brussels') >>> ts Timestamp('2023-01-01 10:00:00+0100', tz='Europe/Brussels') >>> ts.tzname() 'CET'",
    "markdown_length": 485,
